CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_6a26253995dc", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-26mar09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-26mar09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 279137, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "MSVMCU0903    •  Copper prices generally edged up during the month of March, thereby  continuing the mildly bullish trend set in motion during the final week of  February.  By the 23rd, copper broke through the $4000/t barrier for the  first time since November 10th last year.  This provided an opportunity for  more profit-taking on the 24-25th, and prices slipped back to the $3950/t  range.  (See", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_f4e6c55d8ebc", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-27Feb09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-27Feb09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 286050, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "MSVMCU0902    •  Copper’s price patterns during February have generally set the bearish  trends behind most other commodities and mirrored declining equity  market indices.  Ending January on a downward note at $3148/t  ($1.43/lb), LME three-month prices edged up daily through to February 9th,  reaching what has so far been the month’s high of $3561/t ($1.62/lb), or  13% up on that January 30th po", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_11d51213bcd6", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29may09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29may09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 176907, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "MSVMCU0905    •  During the first half of May trading conditions were particularly volatile with  daily min/max variations in 3-month quotes ranging from -$226/t to  +$182/t.  The volatility reflected mixed sentiment and resulted in official   3-month quotes rising from $4491/t at the end of April to $4778/t on the  7th before falling by $455/t to $4323/t on the 14th, which was the month’s  low.  ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_d29f7f53ea57", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30apr09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30apr09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 184610, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "MSVMCU0904    •  During the first half of April official 3-month quotes rose on a daily basis,  barring the 7th, from the month’s low of $4004/t on the 1st to a new   6-month high of $4770/t on the 15th.  The rally was the result of less  negative macroeconomic data, stronger equity prices, ongoing Chinese  buying and tight scrap supply.  However, during the second half of the  month fear over the", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_f14bf0bdf314", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jun09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jun09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 235420, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "MSVMCU0906    •  Thus far in June, official 3-month LME copper prices averaged $5026/t (to  the 29th) up by 10% compared with the May average of $4581/t, the  highest monthly average since September 2008.  Despite the overall  upward trend there were three distinct phases to movements in prices  during the month.  (See pages 2 & 3)  •  So far this year China's uptake of metal units has more than c", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_f9b6254ce116", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30nov09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30nov09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 845541, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper November 2009  •  During November official 3-month quotes rose steadily from the month’s low of $6416/t on the 3rd to the month’s peak  of $6950/t on the 23rd, a new 14-month high.  Whilst prices rose overall it was a month of two halves.  From the start  of the month to the 13th the price was range bound fluctuating between $6580/t at the end of October and $6490/t on  the 12th.  From ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_827f62b77b83", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30oct09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30oct09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 903701, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper October 2009  •  This year’s annual gathering of the metals industry in London during the second week of the month highlighted the  divergence of view on the outlook for copper in the near term.  Market participants from the financial sector appeared  optimistic while those from the physical side were less so.  In the case of the optimists, positive sentiment stemmed  from the belief th", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_b3a3b32f3692", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30sep09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30sep09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 898569, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper September 2009  •  During September official 3-month prices traded within in a relatively narrow range, fluctuating from the month’s high  of $6448/t on the 8th to the month’s low of $5901/t on the 28th.  However, this moderate $548/t overall monthly trading  range masks the fact that day to day volatility has remained a feature of the market with min/max variations in official  3-month", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_dc465c6018a7", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31aug09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31aug09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 395255, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper Metal Service  •  Official 3-month copper prices performed strongly during the first half of August, rising from a low of $5923/t on the 4th  to a peak of $6415/t on the 13th.  However, shortly after mid-month this trend was reversed with 3m quotes (3m)  giving up virtually all of this gain, heading down to $5945/t on the 19th.  Subsequently, renewed impetus has seen  prices driven high", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_750eefe4f826", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31dec09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31dec09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 927758, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper December 2009  •  After a strong finish to November official 3-month prices hit a 15-month high of $7100/t on the 3rd of December and  then retreated briefly to a month low of $6833/t on the 10th.  Since then, 3-month quotes have recovered some of this  lost momentum and are currently hovering around the $6900/t mark.  Market fundamentals, meanwhile, remained  weak with total exchange s", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_d50ce39482a7", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31jul09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31jul09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 264508, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "MSVMCU0907    •  During July official 3-month prices increased sharply, rising from the  month’s low of $4823/t on the 9th to a new 9-month high of $5708/t on  the 31st.  The $885/t price rally represented the sharpest rise in prices  since February last year when prices traded up from $7190/t to $8430/t.   Official prices (3m) averaged $5218/t in July, their highest level since  September last ye", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_3e858dfc6c2c", name_ru: "BrookHunt-economy-Mar09.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2009/BrookHunt-economy-Mar09.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 168586, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "  MSVMEC0903    •  In the US the residential construction market remains in dire straits despite  the unexpected 22% month-on-month increase in housing starts in  February.  On a year-on-year basis starts fell by 47% and permits declined  by 44%.  However, even with the dramatically slower pace of construction  stocks of new homes remain at a record high, equivalent to 13 months of  supply.  A fur", char_count: 17769});
