CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_125f5cbbd7fd", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-4Q2010-16dec10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-4Q2010-16dec10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 888647, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "      Executive summary ......................................................................................................................................................... 3  Demand analysis ............................................................................................................................................................. 4  Overview..................................", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_b3b7b01e8e4d", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-22dec10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-22dec10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 707195, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper December 2010  •  2010 has been a remarkable year for all commodities prices – both hard and softs – and yet as surprising as this may  sound, copper’s anticipated 43% hike in average cash prices this year over 2009 was not even the strongest  performance amongst the LME-quoted metals.  Behind copper’s price strength this year has been support from just  about every cornerstone availabl", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_99075b31d133", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-26feb10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-26feb10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 847038, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper February 2010  •  February’s official 3-month prices were influenced more so by US dollar movements and economic data releases  than by any fundamental factors.  A lack of clear direction in market sentiment was reflected in volatility reaching its  highest level since August last year.  This was evidenced by daily min/max variations in official 3-month quotes  ranging from -$330/t to +", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_c23f5cd2ec0d", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29oct10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29oct10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 694779, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper October 2010  •  On the final two trading days of September, copper prices easily surged past their target level for the month ($8000/t).   Since then quotes for the red metal have remained comfortably above that point for all of October.  However, after  hitting the next target of $8500/t on October 25th, there are some signs that copper could ease back in the very short  term.  •  Aft", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_19ad64c99bf1", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30apr10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30apr10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 853805, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper April 2010  •  April started on a promising note in the wake of the re-emergence of investor risk appetite during the latter stages of  March, with official 3-month prices rising by $129/t to $7971/t on the 6th, their highest level since the end of July  2008.  However, copper, along with most other markets was adversely affected by two events that occurred during  the latter half of th", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_c39cd4407bb0", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jul10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jul10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 701528, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper July 2010  •  While there has been considerably less volatility in copper markets this month compared to June, prices have  generally trended upwards under mildly improving fundamentals or, at least, the impression of such.  Average LME  cash quotes to July 26th edged up by $70/t on June to c.$6600/t, and the closing price of $7126/t on the 26th of this  month was $300/t higher than Jun", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_9661de3aa7a8", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jun10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jun10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 843393, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper June 2010  •  In the absence of any meaningful fundamental market news copper’s fortunes were driven almost entirely by macro- economic events during June.  Volatile trading conditions remained much in evidence with, for example, 3m prices  plummeting earlier in the month by almost $550/t over three consecutive trading days before settling at $6123/t on  the 8th.  Most of this loss was ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_8a696a143ece", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30nov10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30nov10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 703845, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper November 2010  •  All in all, it was a long and hectic ride during a month in which, ultimately, prices have ended up largely where they  began.  That said, we believe that the market has managed to hold ground despite some potentially damaging  fundamentals emerging during the month, and we put this down to a widespread view that, going forward, supply  concerns will continue to shape ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_597586da17ab", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30sep10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30sep10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 698193, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper September 2010  •  Since flirting with cash lows of c.$6000/t ($2.72/lb) in early June, copper prices have responded strongly due to both  constructive fundamentals and some supportive financials, and September’s six-month highs approaching $8000/t  ($3.63/lb) do not appear to be the end of the bull run.    •  Following last year’s near 4% downturn in metal demand, we have noticed a con", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_897068d99e68", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31aug10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31aug10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 771193, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper August 2010  •  Picking up from their rising trend from the end of July, copper prices firmed still further in early August by opening at  $7334/t ($3.33/lb) on the 2nd.  The following week saw the continuation of this upward trend, with cash closing at  $7423/t on the 9th, but new data sets out of China were taken poorly by the market, and swiftly brought an end to the  16-day price ra", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_83d645ffc0e9", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31jan10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31jan10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 885643, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper January 2010  •  Overall official 3-month quotes averaged $5185/t in 2009, down by 25% from 2008’s average of $6883/t.  During the  final months of 2009 prices were supported by supply disruptions resulting from a combination of industrial action and  ongoing wage negotiations as well as by strong economic and demand growth in China.  These factors continued to  be supportive during the", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_c05094dcc190", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31mar10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31mar10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 867998, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper March 2010  •  The closing stages of March saw the return of risk appetite which resulted in official 3-month quotes hitting $7823/t on  the 30th; their highest level since August 2008.  Prior to this, the month was shaping up to be rather directionless with  official 3-month prices trading within a narrow range of just $280/t through to the 26th, compared with $1105/t during  February.", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_396fe437ef8c", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31may10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2010/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31may10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 854782, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper May 2010  •  During May European debt woes took centre stage with the copper market reacting in three distinct phases over the  course of the month.  Initially, between the 4th and the 12th price volatility was much in evidence as nervous trading  conditions saw 3m quotes oscillating above and below the $7000/t mark.  Then, the real panic set in which resulted in  3m copper falling by m", char_count: 20000});
