CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_1b27cdfde2bc", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-4Q2011-15dec11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-4Q2011-15dec11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 940498, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "      Executive summary............................................................................................................................................................. 4  Demand analysis................................................................................................................................................................. 5  Overview............................", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_0df1efb3f198", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-22dec11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-22dec11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 702176, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper December 2011  •  As this is our last copper report of 2011, we would like to take this opportunity of extending our best wishes to our  readers along with our hopes for a prosperous 2012.  This past year will be remembered as a particularly volatile one,  not just for copper, but for most of the commodities markets.  In the case of the red metal, having peaked at $10,148/t  in February", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_516a0512b31b", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-28feb11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-28feb11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 703074, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper February 2011  •  As we noted in our last report, what did indeed turn out to be the January month low copper cash price on the 25th of  US$9330/t ($4.23/lb) now seems to be far away, as the red metal surged upward for the following nine consecutive  trading days to hit a fresh record high.  •  Our overall market balances for 2011 and 2012 have firmed a little since last month’s report ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_113bd1c44cd3", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29apr11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29apr11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 724649, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper April 2011  •  It has been typical during recent metals industry gatherings to see prices move decisively up or down under the  common thread of increasing optimism/pessimism over the week of the meeting itself.  But this time, at CESCO in  Santiago during the first week of the month, copper participants clearly fell into two fairly equal camps of bulls and  bears and, consequently, thi", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_3ce60536333c", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29jul11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-29jul11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 699108, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper July 2011  •  Momentum from the end of June rally on hopes that a Greek tragedy would be avoided carried through into early July  and indeed, through most of the month amid generally positive sentiment.  Certainly, July was not without the odd  negative data point to give the bears something to growl about, but hopes for a workable resolution to Greece’s debt  problems, in addition the ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_bceefa75a4ad", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jun11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30jun11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 698549, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper June 2011  •  Copper continues to be a commodity that is not for the faint hearted as we draw the first half of the year to a close.   For the past two months at least, we have noted the complete lack of conviction behind the metal’s price direction,  and this sentiment has dragged on through June also, with average prices edging upward by a nickel to US$9031/t  ($4.10/lb) (to the 24th)", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_81d62d672e0a", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30nov11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30nov11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 701430, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper November 2011  •  After collapsing in September and then enjoying an impressive recovery at the end of October, price movements over  the past month have resembled more of a controlled bloodletting than the haemorrhaging of two months ago.  Even  though price fluctuations have not been as dramatic as the prior couple of months, they have, however, been  characterised by a general downwa", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_ddc313a0d632", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30sep11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-30sep11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 702730, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper September 2011  •  During a month which has seen strike action by at least three significant-sized copper properties and the promise of  some disruption at a fourth, coupled with reports of rising metal imports by the world’s largest consumer, one would  ordinarily think that copper prices would have strengthened.  But September has proved to be no ordinary month.   Ending August at US$", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_7b18b29ebd19", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31aug11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31aug11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 694043, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper August 2011  •  Just as the talk was returning copper back to the $10,000/t level, economic uncertainty in the shape of renewed  sovereign debt fears in Europe, in addition to concerns over the US debt ceiling, sent copper crashing at the start of  August.  Cash quotes declined by over $1,200/t from the end of July to the low for the month on 10th August before  directionless trade ensu", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_1a60e4b8c935", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31jan11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31jan11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 693136, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper January 2011  •  Copper kicked off the year with a bit of a hangover, declining on a bout of profit taking, in addition to concerns over  Eurozone debt levels and Chinese measures to cool economic activity.  Supply side news then renewed the focus on  the expected market deficit this year and although this sparked considerable interest in seeing five-figure prices the  heat fell away as", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_01111684554f", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31mar11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31mar11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 712345, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper March 2011  •  Natural disasters such as Cyclone Yasi in February and the Japanese earthquake-tsunami earlier this month would  typically bring the type of uncertainty in commodities markets which prompts prices higher out of supply concern.   The immediate market reaction on March 15th – the day the tsunami images were everywhere – was to sell copper,  and it fell by $235/t as the gene", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_0436b6ed3fde", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31may11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31may11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 726469, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper May 2011  •  Last month we noted the lack of direction in copper prices, with as many reasons to be optimistic being negated by  just as many urging for caution.  This month the bears have won out, with LME cash averaging US$8890/t ($4.03/lb)  thus far in May compared with April’s US$9483/t ($4.30/lb).  In our view, this has only been partly driven by the  traditional supply-demand fund", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_9e1e8f7ef80d", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31oct11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly-31oct11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 695456, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper October 2011  •  Having lost a quarter of its value during September it would have been easy to expect that the bloodletting was over  and prices would at least stabilise during October.  Indeed, as meetings and negotiations at LME week underscored  the fact that the world hadn’t as yet ended and that it probably wouldn’t next year either, cash quotes continued to  bounce around.  But i", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_76f4b8dd3774", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-substitution-7feb11.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2011/BrookHunt-Cu-substitution-7feb11.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 93074, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "February 2011    Can copper substitution tame the red dragon as record prices  breathe new fire into debate?  • As the price of copper heads ever skyward, the theme of substitution has come back to the forefront  of market participants’ thinking.  In this Insight we summarise the key drivers of substitution,  highlighting where products have been substituted and what the future might hold.  In sho", char_count: 13057});
