CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_3c0ad2442cca", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly1-31jan12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly1-31jan12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 704208, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper January 2012  •  The start of a new year evidently brought with it fresh optimism as copper prices rallied through the month and broke  through what over the past few months had become a resistance level of c.$8000/t.  The opportunity to take a fresh  look at the fundamentals was perhaps behind a consensus forming that even under a sluggish demand scenario,  despite the implied growth i", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_ca29f3b6ee2e", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly10-31oct12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly10-31oct12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 716274, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "October 2012    Copper October 2012  •  As we incorporate the news gathered during LME week and update Q3 reported production numbers, we have  revised our numbers slightly for this year, but more notably, for 2013.  We have been tracking mine disruptions  closely and incorporating these into our production estimates as the year progressed and it is clear that output growth  has once again disappo", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_06b725e13805", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly11-30nov12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly11-30nov12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 714005, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "November 2012    Copper November 2012  •  Copper prices moved lower over the first couple of weeks of November, as the US elections and the leadership  change in China weighed on the markets.  At the same time exchange stocks continued to pile higher and add further  downward pressure to an already bearish market.  Copper prices have since staged a slow recovery since hitting the  low of $7506 (3-", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_a8baa350b6e5", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly12-21dec12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly12-21dec12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 725738, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "December 2012    Copper December 2012  •  Having rallied some three percent over the course of two trading days at the end of November, the copper price failed  to build on this momentum and cash quotes generally ebbed back and forth around the $8000/t level in the final  month of 2012.  Inevitably, December tends to be characterised by a winding down of activity and a general  reluctance to take ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_7bd05250f231", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly2-29feb12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly2-29feb12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 703666, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper February 2012  •  A strong start to the year quickly ran out of steam when it emerged that Chinese buyers failed to return to the market  post Chinese New Year with quite the gusto that had been hoped.  Indeed, sluggish end use demand has resulted in  firms taking a wait and see approach that was so evident in Europe in the final quarter of last year.  Moreover, with  the arbitrage wind", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_9052a86b407d", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly3-30mar12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly3-30mar12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 700095, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "March 2012    Copper March 2012  •  Copper prices continue to take their cue from a combination of macro-economic news and dollar movement rather  than the fundamentals.  Meanwhile, Chinese copper appetite appears to be in “go slow mode” compounded by rising  inventories and imports.  The key feature of the market is not so much price direction but rather the imbalance in the  location of physical", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_c9bf55d666db", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly4-30apr12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly4-30apr12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 698631, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Copper April 2012  •  Following several months of directionless trading, range bound copper finally succumbed to a meaningful price shift  with cash quotes heading lower from the middle of April on what was perceived as disappointing Chinese trade and  economic data.  The data was of course the symptom (of weak Chinese demand) and not the cause but it was  ultimately concern over the strength ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_56af4d2d8a85", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly5-31may12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly5-31may12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 706444, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "May 2012    Copper May 2012  •  The old adage of “sell in May and go away” seems to be holding true again this year.  The impetus behind the decline  in copper prices has been the resurgence of the Euro crisis and the Greek situation in particular.  The sell off has  been further compounded by long liquidation during the month on both the LME and Comex.  Interest for material is  increasingly subd", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_8c3d07cf4dcb", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly6-29jun12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly6-29jun12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 749884, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "June 2012    Copper June 2012  •  In March we were discussing copper range bound around the $8500/t level.  As the market has moved lower, in  tandem with disappointing macro news, prices are now range bound around the $7500/t level.  The fact that copper  prices have not slipped further and appear for now to be relatively well supported in the face of a raft of broadly  downbeat news, could be vi", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_594041fc7035", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly7-31jul12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly7-31jul12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 719153, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "July 2012    Copper July 2012  •  Weaker equity markets, ongoing worries in Europe and the USA, and as yet limited signs of the anticipated recovery  in China all point to doubts over a second half recovery for copper.  What is clear is that macro news is the driver of  the copper price rather than the market fundamentals.  Expectations are that there may be some more significant  actions on QE an", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_3889d47e9bb0", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly8-31aug12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly8-31aug12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 729752, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "August 2012    Copper August 2012  •  Copper prices spent most of August in a tight range of $100/t either side of $7500/t amid a summer lull in trading  activity.  Prices took their cues predominantly from macro data, although somewhat ironically, downward moves  during the second half of the month were reversed in response to negative data; interpreted as being likely to raise  the likelihood of", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_e5e3e3c79d23", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly9-28sep12.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly9-28sep12.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 707414, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "September 2012    Copper September 2012  •  Copper prices broke out of their prior trading range $100/t either side of $7500/t and moved comfortably above  $8000/t following decisive action from central bankers across the globe, while the potential for a boost to demand  from a major infrastructure spend in China added fundamental fuel to the price fire sparked by easier money.  Copper  held on to", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_c0fe54cc87e7", name_ru: "BH-Economic_December_2012.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/Economics/BH-Economic_December_2012.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 347644, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Economic Focus  Building a recovery   There has been a rapid rise in US house building through 2012, and the last few months in  particular. During October, construction started on 888,000 new houses (annualised rate), the highest number since July  2008 and up by 41% from October 2011. Although this recovery in housing is built upon solid foundations, it is  questionable whether such a pace o", char_count: 11906});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_62d2d3d9d96d", name_ru: "BH-Economic_November_2012.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/Economics/BH-Economic_November_2012.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 368460, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Economic Focus  Current account adds to export woes   In September, Japan’s current account slipped into deficit for the first time in  more than three decades, recording a shortfall of 142 billion yen. The shift in trade balance from surplus to deficit,  following last year’s natural disasters, is well reported but recent developments in the current account raise yet more  concerns about the ", char_count: 11856});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_5e2877d3a637", name_ru: "BH-Economic_October_2012.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2012/Economics/BH-Economic_October_2012.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 349584, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Economic Focus  Catching the global cold    The developed economies of Asia have lost significant momentum over the past few  months. Japan, South Korea, Singapore and Taiwan have all seen their exports weaken as demand from key trade  partners has softened.  With these economies leveraged towards exports, weaker trade is taking its toll on economic  growth – especially manufacturing. In short", char_count: 11264});
