CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_2798c7a3c4a0", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly1-31jan13.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2013/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly1-31jan13.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 766393, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "January 2013    Copper January 2013  •  As we enter the new year, there is an air of cautious optimism as global equities rally and as investors become more  hopeful about economic prospects.  Copper prices continue to benefit from this momentum for now as this market  moves into ‘new’ territory with the onset of what looks to be a period of sustained surpluses as production growth is  set to outs", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_9f5b86962cbc", name_ru: "BrookHunt-Cu-monthly2-28feb13.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2013/BrookHunt-Cu-monthly2-28feb13.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 730508, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "February 2013    Copper February 2013  •  Prices rallied strongly at the start of February, touching a new high for the year of just under $8350/t for 3-month  copper on expectations of a sharp upturn in demand in China.  However, momentum ran out of steam towards the  end of the month on the realisation that it might be better to wait for an actual uptick in consumption before pushing  prices too", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_f2327523f994", name_ru: "Economic_February_2013.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2013/Economic/Economic_February_2013.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 343897, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Economic Focus  Currency wars?   The 20% nominal depreciation of the Japanese yen over the past few months has brought exchange  rates back under the spotlight. Central bankers and political leaders around the world have been quick to decry  competitive devaluations - 'exchange rates should be determined by market fundamentals'. This monthly explores the  market fundamentals that determine exc", char_count: 13083});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_a54ae555a1aa", name_ru: "Economic_January_2013.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2013/Economic/Economic_January_2013.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 345068, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    Economic Focus  Chinese growth bouncing back   China's GDP grew 7.8% in 2012, the slowest annual growth since 1999. While China  seems to be transitioning to a period of structurally slower growth, much of last year’s slowdown was due to cyclical  factors. Looking ahead, the latest data suggest China’s economy is now entering a cyclical upturn; Q4 2012 GDP growth  reached 7.9% year on year, up", char_count: 13115});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_3f7600cc0c66", name_ru: "BH-FirstQuantum-review-9jan2013.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/Brook Hunt/BH-2013/Presentations/BH-FirstQuantum-review-9jan2013.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 900610, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "    A Quantum Leap?  Summary  First Quantum's proposed acquisition of Inmet Mining was first announced in November 2012 – a  transaction valued at ~C$5Bn in equal split of cash and equity. This acquisition would more than double  First Quantum's copper reserves and boost its copper production to become the sixth largest copper  mine producer by 2017 overtaking Rio Tinto. Through Cobre Panama in La", char_count: 14703});
