CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_f60bd4261062", name_ru: "CRU-Cu-wire-monit-3mar10.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/CRU/CRU-2010/CRU-Cu-wire-monit-3mar10.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 746072, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "March 2010    Page 1 of 12  © 2010 CRU International Limited confidential  www.crugroup.com      Recovery Indicators Continue to be Mixed   We have made some minor revisions to our estimates for 2009 and we now believe that  global copper wirerod consumption fell by 7.6% to 12.9 million tonnes. Whilst the fall in  consumption in North America and Europe was around 23%, North East Asia recorded a ", char_count: 20000});
CREATE (:Entity:Publication {id: "doc_736c67d79e2b", name_ru: "CopperChina-stocks-2011Oct20.pdf", path: "Материалы конференций/Источники данных о меди/CRU/CRU-2011/CopperChina-stocks-2011Oct20.pdf", category: "Материалы конференций", ext: "pdf", size_bytes: 175035, sensitivity: "public", confidence: "verified", deep_parsed: true, geography: "International", snippet: "Copper – China and its inventories   The issue of China and the level of copper inventories held in the country remains an ongoing  question.  While many of our clients will have read the recent articles in the press, we are not too  surprised about the level of inventories reported in these articles.  CRU track Chinese copper  inventories closely in association with our China office.  The recent ", char_count: 3588});
